1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,665
Took an advance from a customer?

2
00:00:02,665 --> 00:00:08,250
The UAE e-invoicing guidelines say you invoice it when the money arrives.

3
00:00:08,950 --> 00:00:15,684
Say a contract is worth one million dirhams, with three hundred thousand paid up front.

4
00:00:15,684 --> 00:00:18,470
The advance is invoiced on receipt.

5
00:00:18,470 --> 00:00:24,353
The final invoice is seven hundred thousand plus VAT, not the full million.

6
00:00:25,053 --> 00:00:29,882
That's from the Ministry of Finance's guidelines, version two.

7
00:00:29,882 --> 00:00:32,686
Going live on the first of January?

8
00:00:32,686 --> 00:00:35,101
Check all three in your ERP.

9
00:00:35,801 --> 00:00:40,146
Want a second look at how your ERP handles advances?

10
00:00:40,146 --> 00:00:41,817
Send us a WhatsApp.
